# Shell scripts must have LF endings, always.
#
# A .sh file checked out with CRLF is not a cosmetic problem: a line ending in
# a backslash followed by CR is an escaped carriage return rather than a line
# continuation, so every multi-line command silently splits into pieces.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.php text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.xml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
